Ladybird lays out the fragments of a right-to-left line in logical
order, and now places an empty inline box between two of them where
it is in that order. A box at either end of the line goes to that end
in the line’s direction. In Chrome, Firefox, and WebKit, an empty inline
box between two runs of left-to-right text sits between them, where
the bidi algorithm puts it.

Chrome 157.0.8103.79, Firefox 151.0, and Playwright’s WebKit 26.5 ran
the cases of the test added here, and agree on every one except an empty
box at the end of the line, which Chrome and Firefox put at its left end
and WebKit at its right end; Ladybird matches Chrome and Firefox.
